Let’s face it—there’s something about a fresh coat of paint that makes everything feel new. Whether you’re revamping your living room, giving your kitchen a glow-up, or finally tackling that guest bathroom that’s been stuck in 2009, the right color can completely transform a space. And this year? The paint trends are coming in hot (and cool, and moody, and mellow).
From earthy tones to nostalgic pastels, here are the paint trends we’re absolutely loving in 2025. Get ready to fall in love with your walls all over again.

1. Warm Neutrals Are the New White
Goodbye, sterile grays and clinical whites—2025 is all about warm neutrals. Think creamy beiges, soft taupes, and sun-kissed ivories. These tones make a space feel cozy without overwhelming it. They’re versatile, timeless, and pair beautifully with just about any design style—boho, modern, farmhouse, you name it.
One color we’re seeing everywhere? "Buttered Almond"—a soft, warm beige that makes your home feel like it’s constantly golden hour. Pair it with natural wood and linen textures for instant calm.

2. Moody Blues & Forest Greens
Feeling dramatic? So are we. Deep, moody hues are having a moment—and we’re here for it. Navy blues, forest greens, and charcoal blacks are turning up in home offices, bedrooms, and even powder rooms.
These colors add depth and richness to a space and look especially stunning with brass or matte black hardware. Try "Sapphire Slate" for a bold statement wall or "Pine Grove" for a serene, earthy vibe.
Pro tip: If you’re scared of going too dark, start with an accent wall or a small room like a bathroom. Paint is the ultimate low-commitment makeover—if you don’t love it, you can always repaint!

3. Pastels with Personality
Pastels are no longer just for nurseries. This year’s pastels are all grown up—think dusty rose, muted lavender, and soft pistachio. They bring a gentle pop of color without overpowering a room.
We’re loving "Millennial Mauve" (yes, that’s a thing) in dining rooms and bedrooms for its romantic, vintage feel. And "Mint Condition"? Perfect for a breezy kitchen or bathroom refresh.
The key is choosing shades with a touch of gray or brown in the base to tone down the sweetness and add sophistication.

4. Earth Tones Are Staying Strong
The obsession with terracotta, ochre, and clay-inspired shades isn’t going anywhere. Earth tones bring warmth, grounding energy, and a connection to nature—something we’re all craving in a tech-saturated world.
Colors like "Sienna Clay" and "Golden Ochre" pair beautifully with indoor plants, rattan furniture, and woven textiles. Want to create a cozy reading nook or meditation corner? Earth tones are your best friend.

5. Unexpected Pops of Color
While calm colors are dominating, bold pops are making surprise appearances—especially in unexpected places. Think chartreuse pantries, cobalt blue ceilings, or raspberry red powder rooms.
It’s all about playing and experimenting. Try painting the inside of a bookshelf a bold contrasting color, or give your front door a fresh burst of sunshine yellow. These little doses of color can completely change the mood of a space—and make it uniquely you.

Final Thoughts
The best part about paint trends? You don’t have to follow any of them. Use them as inspiration, mix and match, or throw them out the window and go full neon (we support your creative chaos). At the end of the day, your home should reflect you—your style, your energy, your vibe.
So grab a brush, throw on some old clothes, and have fun with it. Whether you’re channeling cozy cottagecore or bold urban glam, there’s a paint trend waiting to bring your vision to life.
Happy painting! 🖌️✨

